CORE gcc-only
main.c

^EXIT=10$
^SIGNAL=0$
^\[main\.assertion\.1\] line \d+ assertion g == 42: SUCCESS$
^\[main\.assertion\.2\] line \d+ assertion g == 7: SUCCESS$
^\[main\.assertion\.3\] line \d+ assertion c == 2: SUCCESS$
^\[main\.no-body\.__builtin_strlen\] line \d+ no body for callee __builtin_strlen: FAILURE$
--
^warning: ignoring
--
__builtin_strlen is only folded to a constant when its argument has no side
effects. Calls that are not folded remain calls of __builtin_strlen, which has
no body.
